4,"Itneg, Southern in Philippines people group profile | Joshua Project",https://joshuaproject.net/people_groups/15044/RP,"Their musical instruments are the ""kalalent"" (nose flute) the gangsa (copper gongs) and the ""kulintang"" (guitar). The Tinguian are a language group. They are divided into several sub-groups by dialectical differences: Adasen, Binongan, Gubang or Banao, Inlaod - penanubia, Maeng (also called Assa), Masadiit, Moradan, and Mabaca.","Itneg, Maeng",Austronesian
5,Austronesian Music - Music genre - Rate Your Music,https://rateyourmusic.com/genre/austronesian-music/,"Using a zither in the form of a bamboo pipe rounded by strings, called sasando/sasandu/valiha/kolibit as an accompaniment of narrative songs; also other corresponding traditions using different instruments (Sundanese pantun, dayak sape).Austronesian music nowadays refers to the ongoing evolution and fusion of various cultural influences from foreign and neighbouring cultures.","Itneg, Maeng",Austronesian
